## Phase 7: Unified Background Task Dispatcher & Voice Integration
**Goal**: Connect all background workers into HYDRA's master loop in `main.py` so user speech immediately triggers direct workers.

### 7.1 Smart Router Architecture in `main.py`
```python
# HYDRA Direct Background Dispatcher
if is_connected_app_action(cmd_normalized):
    # 1. Check if app has an active direct worker
    worker = DIRECT_WORKER_REGISTRY.get(target_app)
    if worker and worker.is_connected():
        # Execute DIRECTLY in background thread
        result = worker.execute_task(task_type, cmd_normalized)
        speak_voice(result.speech_response)
        return
    
    # 2. Fallback to Autonomous Vision Agent only if direct worker is not connected
    VERIFIED_EXECUTOR.run_vision_agent_task(...)
```

### 7.2 Safety & Privacy Controls
- All credentials and session cookies stored locally in the workspace under AES-256 encrypted storage (`data/vault/`).
- Zero data transmitted to external third-party servers; all API calls go straight from the user's PC to Google, Spotify, or Meta servers.

